<title>GERMANY: Wella says 97 earnings growth on course.</title>
<headline>Wella says 97 earnings growth on course.</headline>
<dateline>DARMSTADT, Germany 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>German haircare-product maker Wella AG said on Wednesday that it expected earnings in the current business year to increase by 25 percent, with sales set to rise by seven percent.</p>
<p>Sales in April were 19 percent higher than in the previous year, while earnings growth thus far had also met expectations, management board chairman Joerg von Craushaar said at the group's annual meeting.</p>
<p>Craushaar said that sales had increased by 10 percent in the first quarter.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
